  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on the first run (5 witnesses, 11 names, composes nothing), so I've finished the session with 5 of the 6 gate runs unused.\n\n**The rule** (`LVMC_11_52_060.lean`):\n- **Who it covers:** a road user in either of the two admitted aggregates, vehicle or trailer.\n- **When it applies:** the road user has been parked for the parameter-set duration (`drv_motion_parked`) and occupies a highway.\n- **What it requires:** for every highway the road user occupies, the curb it stands at, and every travel region it occupies, its reach into the street must be at most `Units.feet 15`. The curb is the road edge of that street nearest its body.\n- **How reach is measured:** distance from the body to the curb, plus length × |cross product of its heading with the region's direction|, plus width × |dot product of the same two|.\n- **Narrowings:** I added none of my own; every reading choice is already in the record's narrowings.\n\n**The witnesses** use a two-lane street with a curb on each side. Each trace has 61 scenes 10 s apart, and the judged window is 200–600 s, so the 180 s parking look-back always falls inside the recording.\n\n| Witness | Scene | Reach (limit 4.572 m) | Expected |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| forbid | truck parked at right angles to the curb | 10.2 m | violated |\n| permit | car parked parallel to the curb | 2.1 m | compliant |\n| idle | car moving at 12 m/s | — | not applicable |\n| blind | as forbid, region geometry masked | unknown | unknown |\n| branch_1 | trailer parked at right angles to the curb | 8.1 m | violated |\n\n**Worth knowing:**\n- The trailer aggregate has no included class, so its half of the class condition can never be true. A trailer only counts because the vehicle aggregate includes `trailer_or_combination`. The gate didn't flag that half as vacuous; it's noted in `task_result.md` as an observation, not a defect report.\n- By mistake I ran one shell command other than the gate (`echo skip`). It changed nothing and didn't use a gate run.\n\n`task_result.md` is in the working directory.",
